## Why This Is Asked
This question probes end-to-end streaming design, practical trade-offs in serialization, transport, exactly-once semantics, schema evolution, and testing under production constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Protobuf schemas and Schema Registry
- Kafka transactions and idempotent producers
- Schema evolution compatibility
- Throughput, latency, partitioning, backpressure
- Replay and recovery strategies
- Monitoring and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Producer initialization with transactions
const producer = new Kafka.Producer({ transactionalId: 'telemetry-producer' });
await producer.initTransactions();
await producer.beginTransaction();
try {
  await producer.send({ topic: 'telemetry', messages: [{ key, value }] });
  await producer.commitTransaction();
} catch (e) {
  await producer.abortTransaction();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test resilience to broker outages and partition rebalancing?
- How do you ensure backward/forward schema compatibility in the registry?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical privacy controls in a real OTCA path, focusing on consent-driven data handling and per-tenant residency.

## Key Concepts
- Ingest pipelines with edge gateways and Kafka
- Privacy controls: redact/drop audio data, store digest only
- Per-tenant residency and retention windows

## Code Example
```javascript
function redact(event) {
  if (!event.consent_opt_in) delete event.audio_payload;
  event.audio_digest = hash(event.audio_payload || '');
  delete event.audio_payload;
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test quota enforcement across tenants?
- How would you monitor privacy policy violations in near real time?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-region data marketplaces under OTCA governance, including residency enforcement, DP budgeting, and auditability.

## Key Concepts

- Data marketplace catalog and policy engine
- Per-tenant residency and epsilon accounting
- Region-scoped streaming and cross-region aggregation
- Immutable audit logs and billing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluation
function evaluateAccess(user, dataset) {
  if (!dataset.policies.includes(user.role)) return false;
  if (Date.now() < dataset.validFrom || Date.now() > dataset.validUntil) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you revoke access and re-compute epsilon budgets in real time?
- How to test utility loss under bursts and evolving policies?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical understanding of lightweight, policy-driven OTCA telemetry for multi-tenant apps, emphasizing real-time decisioning, regulatory retention, and mobility across regions.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant residency and retention controls
- Ingestion-time redaction and field dropping
- Lightweight per-tenant policy engine with dynamic updates
- Edge-to-streaming architecture: edge gateway, regional Kafka, Parquet on S3 with tenant/date partitions
- Privacy, QoS, and policy-change verification

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluator
function evaluate(event, policy) {
  if (policy.drop) return null;
  if (policy.redactUserId) event.user_id_hash = null;
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test policy updates without downtime?
- How would you monitor for privacy violations in production?
